What are macros? In lstc, macros are functions, implemented inside the compiler, they are always available without libraries,
they are always inline.
example:
^section.macro(args);

in future, there will be:
Sections:
Tokenizers /-/ most will tokenize by map, but some will be able to create vocabs themselves
Parsers /-/ parses text
Generators /-/ generates text based on tokens, automatically
IO /-/ handles input and output in console/files
file /-/ advanced file manipulation
http /-/ http communication
sockets /-/ raw connections

btw, macros can be straight assembly, not just lstc code

tips:
if the macros are big & frequently used, then consider wrapping it into a function call so the binary doesn't grow too much
